00:00:05.599 --> 00:00:07.670 align:start position:0%
darkest dungeon is a game about managing  the many stresses of being an adventurer  for hire  fighting undead skeletons investigating  old torture devices and exploring  abandoned crypts is really quite hellish  work and it leaves its mark on the human  psyche this is represented in the game  by a stress meter which is the white bar  below the little red health bar  underneath each character since darkest  dungeon is a turn-based strategy game  you can see our party of the Highwaymen  crusader plague doctor and Vestal is  taking turns unleashing their various  abilities on some pesky skeletons which  abilities they can use isn't determined  by some sort of mana pool or magic  points or anything like that instead  it's all about positioning where each  character is on the lineup is very  important as it determines which  abilities they can use and who they can  attack as you can see here these  skeleton with the shield is a heavy  hitter but can only reach either our  highwaymen or our crusader as those two  are in the front two spots meanwhile our  Vestal and plague doctor are safer in  the back where they can heal and toss  out poisonous grenades respectively now  not all attacks in darkest dungeon deal  physical damage some deal stress damage  instead if a party member gets too  stressed they will either steal their  resolve and keep on fighting or they'll  snap and start panicking a panicked  party member may hide in the back or  push their way to the front and a  murderous frenzy they may attack friends  or take no action at all in short you  have to tend to the minds of your troops  and not just their bodies one way you  can do that is by camping when you camp  in darkest dungeon each character has  camping specific abilities they can use  to help bolster the spirits of either  themselves or the party you can feast on  delicious rations to reduce stress or as  you can see here the vessel is going to  use her prey ability to heal our party's  wounds and reduce their stress after  playing through the demo for darkest  dungeon I found the game to be  reminiscent of XCOM in a lot of ways  both are highly strategic games with an  emphasis on positioning and squad based  tactics and when things start to go bad  they can very very quickly spiral out of  control darkest dungeon is tough but if  you're smart and key  cool head it's not hopeless the  developers hope to have an early access  version of the game out sometime later  this year thanks for watching and I'll  see you all next time
 

